# The sdist carries the tests, so it must carry what the tests need.
#
# 2026-08-12: the zero-resonance regression fixture (the 400-crystal artifact
# that exhibited the grounded-fabrication defect) was absent from the sdist,
# so the guard `pytest.skip`ped for anyone who ran the tests from a released
# tarball. A guard that silently does not run is not a guard — the exact
# failure family the fixture exists to prove we fixed.
recursive-include tests/fixtures *

# 2026-11-14: two more things the shipped tests read from the repo root and
# that the 2.4.1 tarball did not carry, so `pytest` from the sdist failed 2 of
# 674 (test_agents_md_in_sync: FileNotFoundError on AGENTS.md;
# test_formation_gardener::test_migration_script_runs_on_small_corpus: no
# scripts/ dir). Same failure family as above: a test that cannot run from the
# tarball is not a test the tarball's user has.
include AGENTS.md
include scripts/migrate_to_addressed_formations.py
